# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MaghzBook — deployment configuration
# Copy to .env (or export in your shell / CI / app runtime).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the application that serves this bundle.
# EMPTY (default) = all links are internal / relative. Recommended when the
# bundle is served from the same origin as the app (or opened locally).
#
# Set it when assets live on another origin or under a fixed sub-path, e.g.
#   APP_URL=https://books.example.com
#   APP_URL=https://cdn.example.com/maghzbook
#   APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
#
# It is PREPENDED before every internal link:
#   resolve("books/game-theory-strategy/cover.png")
#     -> ""                                  => books/game-theory-strategy/cover.png
#     -> "https://books.example.com"        => https://books.example.com/books/game-theory-strategy/cover.png
#
# Ways to apply it:
#   1. Runtime : window.APP_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_APP_URL  (before page load)
#   2. Build   : APP_URL=https://books.example.com python tools/resolve_urls.py --export ../dist
#   3. Build   : APP_URL=https://books.example.com python tools/resolve_urls.py --in-place
#   4. Node    : const { resolve } = require('./tools/app-url.js'); resolve(path)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_URL=
